2026-09-27  backend/app/services/arduino_cli.py
            Added an OPT-IN guard, VELXIO_SKIP_STARTUP_INDEX, around the
            board-index refresh that the CLI service performs on startup.
            Unset (the default) the upstream behaviour is unchanged. The
            desktop wrapper sets it to 1 because that refresh is a network
            round-trip that runs BEFORE uvicorn binds, blocking the whole
            backend for 44s-150s (measured) and making the app look broken.
            The deferred pass is not lost: ensure_core_for_board() already
            re-runs the same method on demand when a board needs a core
            that is not installed, and an already-installed core
            (arduino:avr) never triggers it.

2026-09-27  backend/app/services/arduino_cli.py
            FIXED an upstream bug in the ESP32 compile path. It passed
            --build-property build.extra_flags=-DARDUINO_ESP32_LCGAMBOA=1,
            but --build-property REPLACES a property and the esp32 platform
            defines build.extra_flags itself (-DESP32, -DARDUINO_ARCH_ESP32,
            the per-board defines). Every one of those was dropped, so any
            library branching on defined(ESP32) took its non-ESP path -
            Adafruit_SSD1306.cpp included <util/delay.h>, which the Xtensa
            toolchain does not ship, and ESP32 builds failed with
            "fatal error: util/delay.h: No such file or directory".
            The defines now go through compiler.cpp/c/S.extra_flags, which
            are empty in the platform and referenced by its recipes, so they
            append instead of replacing. Verified: ESP32-S3 and ESP32-C3
            builds of an Adafruit_SSD1306 sketch now succeed.

            The same pattern in test/backend/integration/test_esp32c3_emulation.py
            was corrected too.

2026-09-27  .gitignore
            Added ignore rules for the desktop wrapper's build output
            (desktop/node_modules, desktop/release, desktop/build/icon.png).

